-- title:
--   Ramification index of X₁(M) over the j-line in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $\kappa\,M$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(M)$ (the field `qExpFunctionFieldC` for the group `Gamma1 M`). Let $J \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC` $\kappa$, that is $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $\kappa$ of the power series $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum`, so $J$ is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Let $x$ be a place of $F$ over $\kappa$, i.e. a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\kappa$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, and let $\operatorname{ord}_x$ denote the associated normalised additive valuation. Assume $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_x J$, and let $j_0 \in \kappa$ be such that $1 \le \operatorname{ord}_x (J - j_0)$. Then $\operatorname{ord}_x (J - j_0)$ equals [`ModularCurve.jWidthChar`](def/ModularCurve_PlaceWidthChar.html#L11) $p\,j_0$, namely: for $p = 2$ it is $12$ if $j_0 = 0$ and $1$ otherwise; for $p = 3$ it is $6$ if $j_0 = 0$ and $1$ otherwise; and for $p \ge 5$ it is $3$ if $j_0 = 0$, $2$ if $j_0 = 1728$, and $1$ otherwise. Of the two hypotheses on $x$, only the inequality $1 \le \operatorname{ord}_x(J - j_0)$ enters the argument.
--
--   This computes the ramification index at an affine place of the function field of $X_1(M)$ over the $j$-line in every characteristic prime to $M$, the characteristic-sensitive table accounting for the extra automorphisms of elliptic curves with $j = 0$ in characteristics $2$ and $3$. It is used in the comparison of orders at places under the $j$-map and in the bound on the number of supersingular $j$-invariants in terms of the index of $\Gamma_1(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_sub_algebraMap_eq_jWidthChar_of_place_x1FunctionFieldC.lean

